Hmm..  Why would one change their own (XML) save files just to post some
score or inventory list?  Why would such a person not just compose these
lists to post?  Even for multi-user environments I cannot see the point,
given the usual access restrictions to the file system.  A cheater does
not need that feature (i.e. XML transfer files), currently, to cheat.

> I think a CRC or MD5-based method is enough and not hard to implement. 

No, both are quite easy to implement, and there are sources available.  So
it is likely that there will soon be a tool for the cheaters to create the 
checksum.

Checksums are to ensure data integrity during transmission (and storage),
not to prevent intended changes.  To prevent intentional changes you'll
need, e.g., MACs (message authentication codes).

